Do not consider SM 8.9 sufficient for FP8 as e.g. NCCL requires SM 9.0, as seen in test_scaled_mm:
>  FP8 reduction support begins with sm90 capable devices.

Author: Alexander Grund (TU Dresden)

diff --git a/torch/testing/_internal/common_cuda.py b/torch/testing/_internal/common_cuda.py
--- a/torch/testing/_internal/common_cuda.py
+++ b/torch/testing/_internal/common_cuda.py
@@ -181,7 +181,7 @@ def evaluate_platform_supports_fp8():
                     return True
             return False
         else:
-            return SM90OrLater or torch.cuda.get_device_capability() == (8, 9)
+            return SM90OrLater
     if torch.xpu.is_available():
         return True
     # As CPU supports FP8 and is always available, return True.
